  "card_notes": [
   "Marker tubes are thin, so one voxel at the tube wall costs a lot of Dice: on four of its own training brains (MF278, MR243, MR257, MR263) the released model reaches Dice 0.75\u20130.85 while its tube volume is within 9 % of the label's. In-plane its tube walls sit within 0.4 mm of the labels' on average; the largest differences are where a tube starts or ends along the cutting axis (up to 0.9 mm, about 2 sections, in MR263).",
   "The shipped rule keeps tubes in the left hemisphere only (it drops voxels at or right of the brain's x-centroid plus 3 voxels), clamps them to the brain mask and drops components under 3 voxels; applied to the 21 training labels it removes 281 of 81,783 tube voxels (0.3 %; 32 of them on the right of that line, the rest outside the brain mask of record), so a brain with tubes in the right hemisphere is outside its scope.",
   "The earlier network (Dataset508) finds much less tube than labelled on 4 of its 5 held-out brains (17\u201352 % of the labelled voxels; MR261 93 %), so it is a weak reference for this task."
  ],
